"catch syscall" on illumos (solnix gdb2, 2026-11-02). Upstream 18.1 has none: sol2 sets no xml_syscall_file and no
get_syscall_number, so every `catch syscall` says "not supported on this architecture yet" (measured on dixi), and the
procfs native target has no set_syscall_catchpoint and only prints "procfs: trapped on entry to ..." for PR_SYSENTRY.
OmniOS/OI ship only the XML (their syscalls.patch adds it to data-directory); nothing in their patch sets reads it.
  - sol2-tdep.c: syscalls/illumos.xml for both ISAs, and a get_syscall_number that is never called (as fbsd/netbsd:
    the native target reports the number from pr_what).
  - procfs.c: set_syscall_catchpoint writes PCSENTRY/PCSEXIT (gdb's own exit/lwp/exec set plus the caught calls, or
    all of them); wait() reports a caught PR_SYSENTRY/PR_SYSEXIT as a syscall entry/return.
  - data-directory/Makefile.in installs illumos.xml, which the recipe generates from the gate proto's sys/syscall.h
    (pkgs/illumos/patches/gdb/gen-syscalls-xml.sh) before configure.

